          Most refrigerators are 30, 33 or 36 inches wide, but the number that decides whether one fits is the one on the spec sheet for that exact model, measured against your opening, your clearances and every doorway on the way in.
        </p>

        <TopPick />

        <div id="by-style" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Standard Refrigerator Dimensions by Style
          </h2>

          <p>
            There is no single standard refrigerator size, but each style falls into a fairly predictable range. Most full-size refrigerators are between 28 and 36 inches wide, 61 and 72 inches tall and 28 and 36 inches deep with the doors and handles included. The table below gives the typical ranges by style. Treat them as approximate planning numbers: every model is different, and the spec sheet for the exact model you are buying is the only number that counts.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Style</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical width</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical height</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical depth (with doors)</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical capacity</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Top-freezer</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">28 to 33 in. (most 30 in.)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">61 to 69 in.</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">28 to 34 in.</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 14 to 21 cu. ft.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Bottom-freezer</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">24 to 36 in. (most 30 or 33 in.)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">67 to 70 in.</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">29 to 34 in.</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 18 to 25 cu. ft.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Side-by-side</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">33 to 36 in.</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">65 to 71 in.</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">28 to 36 in.</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 21 to 28 cu. ft.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">French door</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30 to 36 in. (most 36 in.)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">68 to 72 in.</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">28 to 36 in.</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 20 to 30 cu. ft.</td>
                  </tr>
