          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Standard refrigerator dimensions give you a starting point: about 30 inches wide for most top- and bottom-freezers, 36 inches for most French doors and side-by-sides, and roughly 6 inches less depth for counter-depth models. The exact numbers vary by model, so treat every range here as approximate.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Measure the opening, subtract the clearance the maker asks for, measure every doorway on the way in, and confirm it all against the spec sheet before you order. When you know what fits, our guide to the <a href="/best-refrigerator-brands/">best refrigerator brands</a> will help you choose the model.
          </p>
